# Regional Structure

All code must be organized using regional dividers for clear structure and code folding support.

## JavaScript Regions

```javascript
// #Region[col10] -----
// REGION_TYPE | Description
// -----

    // Content here (4-space indent - CRITICAL for code folding)

// endregion -----
```

**Region Types:** MODULE, FUNCTION, SUB FUNCTION, HELPER FUNCTION, CLASS, METHOD, DATA, CONSTANTS, STATE, API, EVENTS, INITIALIZATION

**Dash Counts:** Opening (60), Section (56 with indent), Closing (50)

---

## CSS Regions

```css
/* -----
 * REGION | Description
 * ----- */

    /* CSS rules (4-space indent) */

/* endregion ---- */
```

**Dash Counts:** Opening/Closing (77)

---

## HTML Regions

```html
<!-- ----- -->
<!-- REGION | Description                                              -->
<!-- ----- -->

    <!-- UI COMPONENT | Description                                   -->
    <!-- --- -->
    <div id="component">
        <!-- Content -->
    </div>
    <!-- --- -->

<!-- endregion ----- -->
```

**Dash Counts:** Opening (65), Subsection (57 with indent), Closing (60)

---

## Rules

### ALWAYS
- Use 4-space indent within ALL regions (critical for code folding)
- Region type in CAPS before pipe separator
- Close every region with `endregion`
- Use correct dash counts per file type

### NEVER
- Skip 4-space indent (breaks code folding)
- Use inconsistent dash counts
- Forget to close regions
- Use tabs instead of spaces
